`g` is passed to `take`, a method: a guard is handed only to a function named at the call, neither a method, a constructor nor a generic, whose parameter is declared as the guard is, `MutexGuard<T>`, once per call, because that parameter is held to the rules of the guard's block; write the helper as `const f = (g: MutexGuard<T>): void => { g.value.n = g.value.n + 1 }` and call it as `f(g)`
